     <h1 class="title" title="Itanagar Hill Station">Itanagar</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/east-india-hill-stations/itangar-hill-station.jpg" title="Itanagar hill station" alt="Itanagar hill station, hill stations in india, east india hill stations, Itanagar" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Arunachal Pradesh<br />
<b>Area:</b> 110 sq.Kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Mini India<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 750m above sea level<br />
<b>Best time to visit:</b> Throughout the year</p>  
<p><b>Main Attractions:</b> Mountains</p>   
<p><b>Itanagar</b> has been the <b>capital of Arunachal Pradesh</b> from April 20, 1974. Itanagar is situated at the foot. The town is located 350 meters above sea level. Is administratively Papumpare district. The Nishi tribe is or ends in the large area of Itanagar. However, Itanagar can be called as <b>mini India</b>, people all over the country, live here in harmony. As capital city of Itanagar is well connected with the rest of the country by road and air communications. <b>Pawan Hans</b> provides helicopter service between Guwahati and Naharlagun (Itanagar). Luxury buses are available from Guwahati. Itanagar is the capital of the largest state in northeastern India. Here you can find strong Itafort historic call data from 14 to 15 centuries, after which he is appointed. The capital of Rajbhawan houses the official residence of the governor also has many places to visit around Itanagar.</p>








